{"h":3395,"lines":[{"w":0.058003807067871116,"h":0.013966972611677786,"c":1,"y":0.10420837413658646,"t":"Test 4","x":0.12943431035803848},{"y":0.1464228503564371,"x":0.12948150293766966,"h":0.017768610492612025,"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","w":0.2904327646891276},{"x":0.12962963815103043,"y":0.18021201465017578,"w":0.77777776082356764,"h":0.018915891928161677,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","c":1},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.19905771515267612,"c":1,"w":0.15843621571858726,"t":"Passage 2 below.","x":0.12962962862063496},{"t":"Silbo Gomero - the whistle 'language' of","h":0.033580031917288977,"c":1,"w":0.5707291158040364,"y":0.22910205315080578,"x":0.23836576599873344},{"h":0.023394485806127019,"w":0.26954732259114583,"y":0.26017441838355437,"t":"the Canary Islands","x":0.3868312768956565,"c":1},{"x":0.12952576018520706,"w":0.74918518066406259,"h":0.019009683382103848,"c":1,"y":0.29753424619928204,"t":"La Gomera is one of the Canary Islands situated in the Atlantic Ocean off the northwest coast"},{"y":0.31511628172773076,"h":0.018714213961004811,"t":"of Africa. This small volcanic island is mountainous, with steep rocky slopes and deep, wooded","c":1,"w":0.7635123697916667,"x":0.12956902777252632},{"y":0.3312546057653305,"c":1,"t":"ravines, rising to 1,487 metres at its highest peak. It is also home to the best known of the world's","h":0.020746078311484339,"w":0.78210332234700508,"x":0.12749076536073034},{"c":1,"x":0.12962962473116987,"y":0.34883720911328742,"w":0.76131688435872391,"t":"whistle 'languages', a means of transmitting information over long distances which is perfectly","h":0.017476100382451065},{"t":"adapted to the extreme terrain of the island.","x":0.12745922191756592,"w":0.35204640706380208,"c":1,"y":0.36568255305132591,"h":0.016777268848935822},{"y":0.39441052070151283,"h":0.023709075891789055,"t":"This 'language', known as 'Silbo' or 'Silbo Gomero' - from the Spanish word for whistle' -","w":0.74519124348958332,"c":1,"x":0.12944110077844886},{"y":0.41557324438757448,"c":1,"x":0.12752799970662096,"t":"is now shedding light on the language-processing abilities of the human brain, according to","h":0.017850707922442366,"w":0.73261164347330732},{"c":1,"w":0.77993855794270828,"h":0.018284760599843963,"t":"scientists. Researchers say that Silbo activates parts of the brain normally associated with spoken","x":0.12751733027120943,"y":0.43134212270449557},{"c":1,"x":0.12747881295907035,"t":"language, suggesting that the brain is remarkably flexible in its ability to interpret sounds as","w":0.73685155232747379,"y":0.44662407106354962,"h":0.021834174651560456},{"c":1,"t":"language.","y":0.46859518951968027,"w":0.0850192387898763,"h":0.014466778830448446,"x":0.12718571909517482},{"t":"'Science has developed the idea of brain areas that are dedicated to language, and we are starting","h":0.016007204359074767,"c":1,"y":0.49852767950328036,"w":0.77572016398111976,"x":0.12962962984129536},{"t":"to understand the scope of signals that can be recognised as language,' says David Corina,","w":0.72222218831380203,"h":0.017667844522968212,"x":0.12757203730400421,"y":0.51442873966301561,"c":1},{"t":"co-author of a recent study and associate professor of psychology at the University of Washington","h":0.019073822192224643,"c":1,"x":0.12955282711105781,"w":0.78410659790039072,"y":0.53136092177862637},{"w":0.085832074483235654,"h":0.015590043736290471,"c":1,"x":0.12891740372093602,"t":"in Seattle.","y":0.54931261715763191},{"y":0.58118911195347789,"c":1,"x":0.12957578045868701,"t":"Silbo is a substitute for Spanish, with individual words recoded into whistles which have high-","w":0.75731745402018236,"h":0.018137338725922381},{"t":"and low-frequency tones. A whistler - or silbador - puts a finger in his or her mouth to increase","x":0.12962962271541595,"y":0.59883720915374439,"w":0.76748972574869812,"h":0.016003780005536927,"c":1},{"t":"the whistle's pitch, while the other hand can be cupped to adjust the direction of the sound. 'There","c":1,"y":0.61434332356321231,"x":0.12956003350681944,"h":0.019197419057605636,"w":0.78615234375000009},{"x":0.12757203586295171,"h":0.017513763778201241,"y":0.63074204959596114,"t":"is much more ambiguity in the whistled signal than in the spoken signal,'explains lead researcher","c":1,"w":0.78600819905598951},{"x":0.12752917780145442,"w":0.77171051025390625,"y":0.64809144567963639,"h":0.018146903551369054,"c":1,"t":"Manuel Carreiras, psychology professor at the University of La Laguna on the Canary island of"},{"w":0.75320109049479167,"h":0.019063322788413717,"c":1,"t":"Tenerife. Because whistled 'words' can be hard to distinguish, silbadores rely on repetition, as","x":0.12957235308812859,"y":0.66414430116512246},{"c":1,"t":"well as awareness of context, to make themselves understood.","h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.49588475545247401,"x":0.12962963867907443,"y":0.68313953473507882},{"w":0.73251027425130211,"y":0.7151162789209663,"x":0.12962963656459911,"c":1,"h":0.016038020171040723,"t":"The silbadores of Gomera are traditionally shepherds and other isolated mountain folk, and"},{"w":0.71810699462890626,"h":0.01598837238037687,"y":0.7325581393886772,"c":1,"x":0.12962963015175252,"t":"their novel means of staying in touch allows them to communicate over distances of up to"},{"x":0.12958065804379648,"t":"10 kilometres. Carreiras explains that silbadores are able to pass a surprising amount of","y":0.74852055637899551,"w":0.70587682088216142,"c":1,"h":0.017303394906231562},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"t":"information via their whistles. 'In daily life they use whistles to communicate short commands,","x":0.12962962266589992,"y":0.76590106019803705,"w":0.76748972574869789},{"c":1,"h":0.019367870649825258,"y":0.78034696669588277,"t":"but any Spanish sentence could be whistled.' Silbo has proved particularly useful when fires have","x":0.12954687063080569,"w":0.77794413248697925},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.12962962232950331,"c":1,"y":0.79941860450432622,"w":0.65843622843424487,"t":"occurred on the island and rapid communication across large areas has been vital."},{"x":0.12962962936976552,"t":"84","w":0.028806584676106778,"c":1,"y":0.92005813934370639,"h":0.01453488398216074}],"w":2400}